⍝ A tour of reading component files.
⍝ Run:  dyalog sample-scripts/component-files/read-data.apls
here←⊃1⎕NPARTS⊃2⎕NQ'.' 'GetCommandLineArgs'
dir←here,'data/'

⍝ Tie (open) a file: you get a tie number, used by every other ⎕F… function
t←(dir,'customers')⎕FTIE 0
(first next bytes)←3↑⎕FSIZE t           ⍝ components are numbered first…next-1
⎕←'customers.dcf: components ',(⍕first),' to ',(⍕next-1),', ',(⍕bytes),' bytes'
⎕←'1: ',⎕FREAD t 1                       ⍝ header text
fields←⎕FREAD t 2                        ⍝ field names
recs←⎕FREAD¨t,¨2+⍳next-3                 ⍝ every record: ⎕FREAD t n for each n
⎕←'' ⋄ ⎕←fields⍪↑recs                    ⍝ records as a table, field names on top
⎕←'' ⋄ ⎕←'total credit limit: ',⍕+/4⊃¨recs
⍝ ⎕FRDCI: who wrote a component, and when (in 60ths of a second since 1970)
(size user time)←⎕FRDCI t 3
⎕←'component 3: ',(⍕size),' bytes, written by user ',⍕user
⎕FUNTIE t

⍝ Orders: each component is a whole namespace
t←(dir,'orders')⎕FTIE 0
o←⎕FREAD t 1
⎕←'' ⋄ ⎕←'order ',(⍕o.id),' for customer ',(⍕o.customer),' on ',o.date,' (',o.status,'):'
⎕←o.lines
orders←⎕FREAD¨t,¨⍳¯1+2⊃⎕FSIZE t
⎕←'orders: ',(⍕≢orders),' · total value: ',⍕+/{+/×/⍵[;2 3]}¨orders.lines
⎕←'by status:' ⋄ ⎕←{⍺,≢⍵}⌸orders.status
⎕FUNTIE t
